  "quote_spans": [
    {
      "chunk_id": 16,
      "char_start": 661,
      "char_end": 1047,
      "text": "Salve had\nthe middle watch; and by that time the sea was running high, and they\nwere plunging through the darkness under a double-reefed mainsail, the\nmoon every now and then clearing an open space in the storm--clouds that\nwere driving like smoke before it, so that he could fitfully distinguish\nobjects over the deck, even to the look-out man's looming figure out\nupon the forecastle"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 80,
      "char_start": 442,
      "char_end": 959,
      "text": "He was as black as a negro from the coal-dust,\nand declared tremblingly when he came up on deck, that he had deserted\nfrom his regiment in Monte Video, which was an offence punishable by\ndeath, and that he had thought he might remain concealed until the\nvessel arrived at Rio; that he had come on board in the dark on the last\nevening they lay in the harbour, and had hidden himself under the coals;\nand that when they had battened down the hatch he had been nearly\nsuffocated with coal-gas, and had lain and groaned"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 81,
      "char_start": 1006,
      "char_end": 1372,
      "text": "Before a light afternoon breeze they glided at last from the sea into\nthe narrow channel that runs up to Rio de Janeiro--one of the loveliest\nin the world, with majestic granite mountains on either side, one of\nwhich was already blazing in the ruddy light of the evening sun, while\nthe other in shade stood out a deep violet against the clear blue of the\nsky above"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 82,
      "char_start": 1244,
      "char_end": 1742,
      "text": "The harbour pilot, however--a consequential Mulatto in a Panama hat and\nred feather, and decorated with a badge and staff--was more\nsharp-sighted, and soon perceived, from the irritable tone in which the\nsong at the capstan was sung again as they warped the vessel round to\nher anchorage in the Ilha das Cobras basin, that there was discontent\nprevailing on board; and it was no doubt owing to a hint from him that\nalready the same evening there were \"runners\" waiting about near them on\nthe quay"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 84,
      "char_start": 275,
      "char_end": 719,
      "text": "Before leaving the vessel Salve placed his silver watch, on which he had\nscratched with the point of his knife, \"In remembrance of Salve\nKristiansen,\" in the waistcoat pocket of Nils, who was snoring loud and\nlong in his hammock alongside; and then, unobserved by the watch on\ndeck, the two friends clambered over to the quay in the silent night by\nmeans of the shore rope, and disappeared at once into the darkness of\nthe neighbouring alleys"
    }
  ],
